    "updated_at": "2019-10-28T01:08:13Z",
    "body": "I love this idea. I'll try to work on this over the coming week but I'd like some feedback for platform specific config locations (in order of files read. files read later will overwrite previous files):\r\n\r\n### Linux:\r\n* [XDG](https://specifications.freedesktop.org/basedir-spec/basedir-spec-latest.html)\r\n  1. iterate over $XDG_CONFIG_DIRS, overwriting previous files in the order the environment variable is set.\r\n  2. $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/starship.toml\r\n* alternative config spec? just use /etc/starship.toml + ~/.config/starship.toml?\r\n### BSD:\r\n* [FreeBSD Handbook](https://www.freebsd.org/doc/handbook/configtuning-configfiles.html)\r\n  1. /etc/starship.toml\r\n  2. /usr/local/etc/starship.toml\r\n  3. ~/.config/starship.toml\r\n### Mac:\r\nfollow BSD?\r\n### Windows:\r\n???\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nAlternatively, should starship just copy the functionality of git's `git config --list --show-origin`, minus the ./.git/config file (I think this is the source code for it: https://github.com/git/git/blob/b5101f929789889c2e536d915698f58d5c5c6b7a/builtin/config.c#L179)? ",
    "author_association": "NONE",
