    "updated_at": "2019-11-03T06:01:30Z",
    "body": "I would like to add to the suggestion a scanning of config file overrides from PWD upwards. That would be done with `.starship.toml` files in any directory.\r\n\r\nThe use case is that while doing work related stuff, I have the Kubernetes and AWS modules displaying valuable information. However, when not doing work stuff, these modules clutter my prompt. The idea would be to disable both of these in the ~/.config/starship.toml file, and add a `.starship.toml` file in the \"work\" projects directory that enables these two modules.\r\n\r\nIf there's going to be any configuration merge mechanism, it can as easily work with any number of files. However, it might have performance impact, considering that starship is stateless and needs to reload configs every time.",
