    "body": "@freelock I agree it seems bad especially for something that can run arbitrary code every time someone hits enter.\r\n\r\nI'm guessing at @nomaed's intent here, but I think they meant it as something similar to how git can be configured per-project with .git/config and .git/hooks? But I agree, there's a reason those files can't be just checked into a repo without a lot of extra, manual work.\r\n\r\nBut I don't want to fully poo-poo the idea outright either. I think I'll continue to try to add the functionality as initially requested and the additional functionality can be debated later. Perhaps what @nomaed needs is not per-folder config, but perhaps better config over how the modules (in particular AWS and k8s) run in the first place? Perhaps a whitelist/blacklist of what folders to care about is more appropriate?",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
