    "updated_at": "2019-11-04T07:46:12Z",
    "body": "> I'd be curious what scenario you have in mind, for searching in the current directory... my initial reaction is to shudder at the security implications of this...\r\n\r\nI didn't think of the security aspect really. I thought of examples such as npm's .npmrc, but now that I looked at its spec, it seems that I was wrong about how it works. \r\n\r\nI am not familiar enough with how startship does things, so I didn't image that it can cause arbitrary code execution as @marblenix suggested. I was thinking of it only as configuration parameters. But I definitely see the point.\r\n\r\nThe idea was to make something more generic than adding more customization properties to specific modules. Perhaps an include/exclude (or whitelist/blacklist) option for root module config can be added, in which a list of paths (with wildcards hopefully) can be provided, and it can control when a module gets enabled or disabled. Of something like git's `includeIf` that if the project is in a specific directory, you can include an additional configuration overriding .gitconfig file.\r\n\r\nBut at any rate, this is definitely an off-topic for this issue, so I might think about it some more and create a new suggestion :)",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
