    "updated_at": "2020-01-05T16:28:04Z",
    "body": "(this is def following a tangent away from the OP's issue:) but this seemed like the place to ask the security question)\r\n\r\n> I am not familiar enough with how startship does things, so I didn't image that it can cause arbitrary code execution.\r\n\r\nYeah interesting! @marblenix can you say more about the security risk you see being introduced by (my understanding of nomaed's idea)\r\n\r\n```\r\n/etc/starship.toml\r\n/usr/local/etc/starship.toml\r\n~/.config/starship.toml\r\n$PWD/starship.toml\r\n```\r\n\r\nor even, since Starship supports Git and Mercurial modules,\r\n\r\n```\r\n/etc/starship.toml\r\n/usr/local/etc/starship.toml\r\n~/.config/starship.toml\r\n$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)/startship.toml or $(hg root)/starship.toml if relevant\r\n$PWD/starship.toml\r\n```\r\n\r\nthat isn't already there with\r\n\r\n```\r\n/etc/starship.toml\r\n/usr/local/etc/starship.toml\r\n~/.config/starship.toml\r\n```\r\n\r\nor even with just having a custom prompt script?\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n\\* I suppose might want to read $PWD/starship.toml only if that file wasn't already read earlier by /etc/starship.toml etc? New to Rust, don't know what the most performant approach would be",
