    "updated_at": "2020-05-29T02:09:35Z",
    "body": "For Unix I think more ideally it would be `${PREFIX}/etc/starship.toml` - using the env var set at compile time, if available.  Then it can be in `/`, `/usr/local`, `/usr/pkg` or `/opt` or wherever else the package system or user might want it.\r\n\r\nTo quote the [FreeBSD *porters* handbook](https://www.freebsd.org/doc/en_US.ISO8859-1/books/porters-handbook/porting-prefix.html):\r\n\r\n> `PREFIX` determines where the port will be installed. It defaults to `/usr/local`, but can be set by the user to a custom path like `/opt`. The port must respect the value of this variable.",
